      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Small molecule mitohondrial uncouplers transport protons from the mitochondrial inner membrane space into the mitochondrial matrix independent of ATP synthase, uncoupling nutrient metabolism from ATP generation. The therapeutic potential of mitochondrial uncouplers have been investigated for the treatment metabolic diseases such as obesity and type 2 diabetes (T2D), as well as for neurodegenerative diseases including Alzheimer's disease and Parkinson's disease. This perspective will review the mitochondrial uncouplers reported to date and explore their potential as therapeutics."},
